r</surname><given-names>Anand</given-names></name><name><surname>Dhaen</surname><given-names>Christoffel</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Marius Fieschi, Enrico Coiera, Yu-Chan Jack Li</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Ontology-based error detection in SNOMED CT</article-title><source>MEDINFO 2004 &#x02013; Proceedings of the 11th World Congress on Medical Informatics Studies in Health Technology and Informatics</source><year>2004</year><volume>1</volume><publisher-name>San Francisco, CA, USA, Amsterdam: IOS Press</publisher-name><fpage>482</fpage><lpage>486</lpage><comment>September 7&#x02013;11, 2004</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cimino</surname><given-names>James J</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhu</surname><given-names>Xinxin</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The practical impact of ontologieson biomedical informatics</article-title><source>IMIA Yearbook of Medical Informatics</source><year>2006</year><publisher-name>Stuttgart: Schattauer</publisher-name><fpage>124</fpage><lpage>135</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Spackman</surname><given-names>Kent A</given-names></name><name><surname>Reynoso</surname><given-names>Guillermo</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Udo Hahn, Stefan Schulz, Ronald Cornet</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Examining SNOMED from the perspective of formal ontological principles: Some preliminary analysis and observations</article-title><source>KR-MED 2004 &#x02013; Proceedings of the 1st International Workshop on Formal Biomedical Knowledge Representation, Collocated with the 9th International Conference on the Principles of Knowledge Representation and Reasoning (KR 2004), Whistler, BC, Canada, June 1, 2004</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>Bethesda, MD: American Medical Informatics Association (AMIA)</publisher-name><fpage>72</fpage><lpage>80</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://CEUR-WS.org/Vol-102/"/></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Heja</surname><given-names>Gergely</given-names></name><name><surname>Surj&#x000e1;n</surname><given-names>Gy&#x000f6;rgy</given-names></name><name><surname>Varga</surname><given-names>P&#x000e9;ter</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ontological analysis of SNOMED CT</article-title><source>BMC Medical Informatics and Medical Decision Making</source><year>2008</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>S8</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schulz</surname><given-names>Stefan</given-names></name><name><surname>Mark&#x000f3;</surname><given-names>Korn&#x000e9;l</given-names></name><name><surname>Suntisrivaraporn</surname><given-names>Boontawee</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Formal representation of complex SNOMED ct expressions</article-title><source>BMC Medical Informatics and Medical Decision Making</source><year>2008</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>S9</fpage></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>